Z||000000||JohnnyK||09-05-2000||05:39 PM||||Well, when I pulled the line down, it almost snapped clean in half in the part I thought it might be leaking from. I Hope this is the problem. But anyways, to anyone who has done this or can take the time to look at this, the clutch line is attached by to rubber things (about midway under the car, right near the edge of the drivers side) and the rubber things go over a metal pipe (coolant?). Anyways, the part where the rubber goes over the metal is really, really coroded (Only seems to be corroded where the leak was) and the rubber will not stay. Am I safe to hose clamp the steel clutch line to the metal coolant line? (Maybe just hose clamp over the rubber to keep it on there). Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||09-05-2000||05:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>One more question<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I don't believe that for a second... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'm not familiar with how the line is held in place, but I definitely wouldn't clamp it metal to metal next to a coolant tube or to anything metal for that matter. However, you better get a second opinion from someone who has had a better look at their hydraulic line than I have.||||reg||6
