Z||000012||JohnnyK||09-06-2000||10:47 AM||||On the newsgroup, someone said that instead of flexible line, you can coil the brake line a bunch of times right before the slave cylinder... Any thoughts on this?||||reg||1
Z||000013||wilburt||09-06-2000||11:39 AM||||Like Patrick said, you need that flexable line. The metal line coming from your master cly. is attached solidly to your frame. Your engine,cradle,trans. AND slave cly., are moving, vibrating, shaking with engine running. With a coil of metal line moving, vibrating, shaking, in short order, will be squirting fluid very soon.  <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000014||JohnnyK||09-06-2000||01:15 PM||||Well, I have brake lines all over the city being assembled (one side is at the hydraulic place, getting the hydraulic line attached for the slave. The other side is getting bubble flared (I hope he said bubble and not double) and the attachment put on. I have to join them in the middle with a coupler or two though. And I don't have the flexible hose near the master, btu I don't see the point in that anyways..||||reg||1
